descriptionByLocale.en:
At Roche you can show up as yourself, embraced for the unique qualities you bring. Our culture encourages personal expression, open dialogue, and genuine connections, where you are valued, accepted and respected for who you are, allowing you to thrive both personally and professionally. This is how we aim to prevent, stop and cure diseases and ensure everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Join Roche, where every voice matters.

The Position
Roche Kaiseraugst is a cornerstone of Roche’s global manufacturing and logistics network. More than 1,900 people are employed at this site, which houses Roche’s largest and most innovative packaging facility worldwide.

The QC Packaging Speed Testing group is part of the QC PMD organization and ensures the high-quality standards of primary and secondary packaging materials used in our manufacturing operations. As an Intern in the Packaging Speed Testing team, your main responsibilities will include leading sub-projects and supporting organizational development.

The Opportunity
You will collaborate with key interfaces such as Quality Assurance, Laboratories, Supplier Quality Management, Packaging Development, Warehouse, Procurement, and Planning. This provides you with a broad insight into the work of the Quality Unit and the production center.

You will actively support the Packaging Speed Testing team in day-to-day operations and current projects. In the process, you will learn how to apply Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) requirements in a practical setting and build solid project management expertise.

Your tasks will include:

• Leading and managing sub-projects;

• Supporting organizational development initiatives;

• Introducing gamification elements;

• Contributing to process optimization;

Who You Are
You are open to new ideas and not afraid to challenge conventional thinking. You enjoy working in a performance-driven environment shaped by mutual respect, open dialogue, and collaboration. Roche offers you a dynamic, international setting with numerous development opportunities.

In addition, you…

• Are a university student in psychology, innovation, or a scientific field, currently enrolled or graduated within the last 12 months;

• Are motivated to conduct research on gamification and failure culture;

• Have an organized and structured way of working;

• Have strong spatial reasoning skills;

• Are team-oriented and have a communicative personality;

• Possess a high level of initiative, assertiveness, and persuasiveness;

• Are reliable and detail-focused; additional experience in a GMP-regulated environment is a plus;

• Are proficient in MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint);

• Possess excellent German and good English skills.

Additional Information

• Preferred start date for the internship is November/December 2026, with a duration of 6-12 months.

• Please note that, due to regulations, non-EU/EFTA citizens must include a confirmation from their university that the internship is a mandatory part of their curriculum with their application documents.

Ready to take the next step? We'd love to hear from you. Apply now to explore this exciting opportunity!

Who we are
A healthier future drives us to innovate. Together, more than 100’000 employees across the globe are dedicated to advance science, ensuring everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Our efforts result in more than 26 million people treated with our medicines and over 30 billion tests conducted using our Diagnostics products. We empower each other to explore new possibilities, foster creativity, and keep our ambitions high, so we can deliver life-changing healthcare solutions that make a global impact.

Let’s build a healthier future, together.

Roche is an Equal Opportunity Employer.

